{
  "story_id": "S011",
  "title": "CHD8 loss produces a caudal neuronal Pnisr/Usp11/Dus3l-down and Csf2ra/Aaas-up state",
  "status": "grounded",
  "rejection_reason": null,
  "exact_observed_result": "Chd8 knockdown was strongest in 151 TH Prkcd Grin2c Glut, 155 MB Glut, and 191 MB P MY GABA. In the leading 151 TH class, Chd8 was depleted with logFC -0.5318986177444458 and FDR 1.0221595465910485e-09 while Pnisr, Usp11, and Dus3l fell and Csf2ra and Aaas rose; the same Pnisr/Usp11/Dus3l-down core recurred in 155 MB Glut and 191 MB P MY GABA.",
  "biological_interpretation": "Acute CHD8 loss in the profiled adult mouse brain is not a uniform cortical Wnt/cell-cycle state; it exposes a posterior neuronal RNA-processing-like abundance module that is most resolved in thalamic, midbrain, and hindbrain classes.",
